      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Kustomize splits it in two. The base holds everything the copies share. Ours has been there since Episode 2, in manifests/base."
        },
        {
          "text": "Each environment gets an overlay: a small folder that points at the base, and says only what's different."
        },
        {
          "text": "Kustomize reads an overlay, applies its changes to the base, and prints ordinary YAML. It's built into kubectl, so there's nothing to install.",
          "say": "Kustomize reads an overlay, applies its changes to the base, and prints ordinary YAML. It's built into cube control, so there's nothing to install."
        },
        {
          "text": "There are no templates, unlike the Helm charts from Episode 7. The base is real YAML that would apply on its own, and overlays patch it.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
