      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "One trap. The namespace setting changes namespace fields, but not text inside values. And our config spelled out the database's full name, namespace and all."
        },
        {
          "text": "So a dev pod would have connected to the prod database, and every test link would land among the real ones."
        },
        {
          "text": "Nothing would have failed. That's what makes it dangerous."
        },
        {
          "text": "The fix is in the base: the short name, postgres-0.postgres. DNS inside a pod tries its own namespace first, so each copy finds its own database.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "prod-apply",
      "type": "terminal",
      "title": "~/k8s-videos",
      "steps": [
        {
          "at": 0,
          "command": "kubectl diff -k manifests/overlays/prod | grep '^[-+] ' | sort | uniq -c",
          "output": [
            "      1 +  DATABASE_HOST: postgres-0.postgres",
            "      1 -  DATABASE_HOST: postgres-0.postgres.golinks.svc.cluster.local",
            "     11 +    environment: prod"
          ]
        },
        {
          "at": 3,
          "command": "kubectl apply -k manifests/overlays/prod | awk '{print $2}' | sort | uniq -c",
          "output": [
            "     11 configured"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "Prod first, since it's already running. kubectl diff, with the k flag for Kustomize, shows what an apply would change. Here filtered to just the changed lines.",
          "say": "Prod first, since it's already running. Cube control diff, with the K flag for Kustomize, shows what an apply would change. Here filtered to just the changed lines."
        },
        {
          "text": "Two kinds of change. The database host becomes the short name, and all eleven objects get the new label."
        },
        {
          "text": "The running pods keep the old host until they next restart. Both names reach the same database here, so that's harmless."
        },
        {
          "text": "Apply with the same k flag. Everything says configured: only labels and one config value changed, so nothing restarts.",
          "say": "Apply with the same K flag. Everything says configured: only labels and one config value changed, so nothing restarts.",
          "pauseAfter": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
